  "name": "Convocator Companionship",
  "type": "feat",
  "effects": [],
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p class=\"Standard\">Your convocator grows more powerful through your journey, though how they grow is dependent on the nature of your companionship:</p><ul><li><p class=\"Standard\">If your convocator is an animal companion or similar, you gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.yozSCfdLFHVBbTxj]{Mature Animal Companion} feat (or an equivalent for a different type of companion). When you Sustain Domain Convocation, you also Command an Animal.</p></li><li><p class=\"Standard\">If your convocator is a familiar, you gain the @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.feats-srd.N7dTFxpjXGn4ddq8]{Enhanced Familiar} feat. When you Sustain Domain Convocation, you also Command your familiar.</p></li><li><p class=\"Standard\">If your convocator is an eidolon, when you Sustain Domain Convocation your Eidolon can Stride or Strike. Using the Sustain action in this way grants it the Tandem and Traversal trait.        </p></li></ul>"
    },
